# /etc/desktop.icons — scene-file DE desktop launcher icons.
#
# ⚠ NOT CURRENTLY READ (verified 2026-08-03, 1.0). /bin/hamdesktop builds
# the desktop from ~/Desktop/*.desktop via the shared directory scanner;
# this path survives only in hamdesktop.ad COMMENTS, with no code behind
# them. The entries below do not match what renders, in either direction.
#
# Kept rather than deleted because removing shipped config is a behaviour
# change, and because the format below is still the intended shape if the
# read path is restored. If you are looking for what the desktop actually
# shows, look in ~/Desktop/.
#
# The original contract, for reference. One launcher per non-blank,
# non-'#' line:
#
#     label|type|action
#
#   label  : text drawn under the icon
#   type   : "folder" -> folder glyph; anything else -> document glyph
#   action : an absolute path. A /bin/* path is SPAWNed (its own window);
#            any other path is treated as a directory and opened in the
#            file manager AT THAT PATH. A leading `~` expands to the
#            session user's home (resolved from $HOME, else the desktop
#            dir's parent) — so this file is correct both on the live
#            image (`live`) and on an installed system whose regular
#            account the installer wizard named.
#
# If this file is absent or empty, hamdesktop falls back to a built-in
# default set (Files / Terminal / Home).
Files|folder|/bin/hamfmscene
Terminal|file|/bin/hamtermscene
Calculator|file|/bin/hamcalcscene
Text Editor|file|/bin/hameditscene
Input Inspector|file|/bin/haminput
Install Hamnix|file|/bin/haminstallui
Control Center|file|/bin/hamctl
System Monitor|file|/bin/hammonscene
Calendar|file|/bin/hamcalscene
Notes|file|/bin/hamnotesscene
Log Viewer|file|/bin/hamlogscene
Word Processor|file|/bin/hamwrite
Spreadsheet|file|/bin/hamsheet
Presentation|file|/bin/hamslides
Home|folder|~
